1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:06,670
Let’s set up a new CateringMS workspace. Here’s how Cedar and Sage Catering gets ready to take its first booking.

2
00:00:07,620 --> 00:00:14,070
Start with your company name and contact details. Add your legal and registration details if they apply.

3
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:21,370
Enter your kitchen or dispatch address so your team has the right starting point for delivery distances and routing.

4
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:27,230
Add your logo and brand colours. This gives the customer portal your company’s look.

5
00:00:28,187 --> 00:00:35,607
If you accept bank transfers, add your business banking details for EFT. You can also come back to this later.

6
00:00:36,553 --> 00:00:42,663
If you take online payments, connect your company’s own payment provider. You can skip this while you’re getting set up.

7
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:49,050
Set whether you’re VAT registered so CateringMS can use the appropriate invoice heading.

8
00:00:49,987 --> 00:00:55,267
Use the shared CateringMS sender to get started, or set up and verify your own domain.

9
00:00:56,220 --> 00:01:01,840
Choose which alerts your team needs, and set up push notifications on the device you want to use.

10
00:01:02,787 --> 00:01:07,517
Review payment due dates and reminders, then decide which automatic emails to turn on.

11
00:01:08,453 --> 00:01:12,943
Already have a customer list? You can import your contacts in bulk or add them later.

12
00:01:13,887 --> 00:01:20,467
Select Finish setup and go to dashboard. Optional integrations like WhatsApp can wait until you’re ready.

13
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:28,940
Your workspace is ready for the next step. Use the dashboard checklist to keep setting up your team and get ready for your first quote.
